# Modularity

- Keep code coherent and reviewable. Split large components when it simplifies testing, ownership or changes; do not require an unrelated refactor before making a focused fix.
- Preserve stable public APIs and transitive dependency behavior.
- Prefer explicit types, clear boundaries, and small reversible edits over large rewrites.
- Use measured evidence rather than blanket 200/400-line bans. When a file is difficult to understand, document and address the actual cause.
